What is a Kafka Consumer Group? Why do we need Consumer Groups?
"A Kafka Consumer Group is a group of consumers that work together to consume messages from a Kafka topic.

We use consumer groups to achieve parallel processing and scalability.

In an e-commerce application, the Order Service publishes an OrderCreated event. Payment, Inventory, and Notification services subscribe using three different consumer groups.

Each consumer group independently receives and processes the event according to its business requirements. This allows multiple services to process the same event without depending on each other."
